>>> IPv6 connection track and IPv6 stack separately use a different que=
ue to=20
>>> manage received fragments. The former uses nf_ct_frag6_queue struct=
ure,=20
>>> the latter uses frag_queue structure.
>>>
>>> When creating new queue for IPv6 connection track, ip6_frag_init()=20
>>> that belongs to IPv6 stack is called to initial nf_ct_frag6_queue s=
tructure.=20
>>> This broken the saddr&daddr member in nf_ct_frag6_queue, and then h=
ash value=20
>>> generated by nf_hashfn() is not equal with that generated by fq_fin=
d().=20
>>> So, a new received fragment can't be inserted to right queue.
>>> =20
>>> The patch fixes the bug with protocol-related initialization routin=
e.
>>> The patch-set have been tested.
>>>
>>> Signed-off-by: Shan Wei <shanwei@cn.fujitsu.com>
>> This breakage was recently introduced by:
